00:40:48.999 --> 00:40:52.570
And that issue has to do
with the determination

00:40:52.570 --> 00:40:55.110
of the magnitude of value, right?

00:40:55.110 --> 00:41:00.110
And is the magnitude of value
socially necessary labor time,

00:41:00.320 --> 00:41:05.320
is that determined entirely in production,

00:41:05.910 --> 00:41:09.980
or also at least in part
in exchange and depends on

00:41:10.870 --> 00:41:15.630
the demand on the market
for individual commodity,

00:41:15.630 --> 00:41:18.585
so this is really one of the
most controversial issues

00:41:18.585 --> 00:41:23.585
among Marxian economists in
general in recent decades.

00:41:24.335 --> 00:41:28.060
Michael's interpretation as I understand,

00:41:28.060 --> 00:41:32.490
it comes out of the
(indistinct) reading in Germany,

00:41:32.490 --> 00:41:35.123
which has evolved in
the rest of the world,

00:41:36.602 --> 00:41:39.083
in terms of value form,

00:41:40.810 --> 00:41:45.810
the so-called value form,
interpretation of Marx's theory,

00:41:46.130 --> 00:41:49.030
this so-called value form

00:41:49.030 --> 00:41:53.320
interpretation has become
popular in recent decades.

00:41:53.320 --> 00:41:57.420
And its proponents argue that
socially necessary labor time

00:41:57.420 --> 00:42:00.150
is not determined solely
by average labor time

00:42:00.150 --> 00:42:02.271
in production, but also depends

00:42:02.271 --> 00:42:06.090
in part on social demand on the market.

00:42:06.090 --> 00:42:11.000
And Michael is a prominent proponent

00:42:11.000 --> 00:42:14.196
of this value form interpretation

00:42:14.196 --> 00:42:17.130
Michael wrote in the introduction

00:42:17.130 --> 00:42:21.150
in his introduction to "Capital" book,

00:42:21.150 --> 00:42:24.030
labor time expended in production

00:42:24.030 --> 00:42:26.937
as well as for the satisfaction

00:42:26.937 --> 00:42:31.103
of monetary social
demand, constitutes value.

00:42:32.860 --> 00:42:34.256
Turning the sentence,

00:42:34.256 --> 00:42:37.180
value is constituted both

00:42:37.180 --> 00:42:41.470
by the labor expended in production

00:42:41.470 --> 00:42:45.183
and the satisfaction of monetary demand.

00:42:46.970 --> 00:42:48.936
So first I wanna review again,

00:42:48.936 --> 00:42:52.420
some of the main passages in chapter one,

00:42:52.420 --> 00:42:53.969
that support my interpretation,

00:42:53.969 --> 00:42:57.278
that socially necessary labor time

00:42:57.278 --> 00:42:59.833
is determined by production.

00:43:01.170 --> 00:43:02.880
- Could I interrupt you for a sec?

00:43:02.880 --> 00:43:03.713
- [Fred] Yeah.

00:43:03.713 --> 00:43:07.688
